      "sample_index": 2,
      "text": "We begin by noting the properties of a circle and its tangents:  the radius of the circle is perpendicular to the tangent at any point on the circle.  The key observation is that $\\angle OBE = \\angle OCE$ because both angles are inscribed angles subtending the same arc $BP$.\n\nNext, recall that $\\triangle BOC \\cong \\triangle BAC$ since they share the same vertex angle $\\angle BAC = \\angle BOC$ and have a pair of equal angles (vertical angles).  Thus \\[\\angle OBE = \\angle BCO = \\angle OCA = \\angle OCE\\] and \\[\\angle BEC = \\angle BAC = \\angle OEA = 47^\\circ\\]\n\nFinally, we contribute $\\angle CED = \\angle CEB + \\angle BEC = \\angle OCE + \\angle OEA = \\angle OOC = 90^\\circ,$ as illustrated in the diagram below.\n\nWe already know $\\angle BAC = 47^\\circ$ and since $AO$ is a radius, $\\angle OAB = \\angle OBA = \\frac{1}{2}\\angle BAC = 23^\\circ$. Since $\\angle BAE = 43^\\circ$, $\\angle OAE = 60^\\circ$. Hence, $\\angle OED = 23^\\circ + 60^\\circ = 83^\\circ$, and it follows that $\\angle CED = 90^\\circ$.\n\nTherefore, the answer is $\\boxed{90}$ degrees. The answer is 90",
