      "text": "The tangent at $B$ is perpendicular to the radius $OB$, so $\\angle BOC = 90^\\circ$.\nSimilarly, the tangent at $E$ is perpendicular to the radius $OE$, so $\\angle EOD = 90^\\circ$.\nSince $AB$ is a diameter, $\\angle AOB = 90^\\circ$.\nIn triangle $AOB$, we have $\\angle AOE = 180^\\circ - \\angle AOB = 90^\\circ$.\nThen, $\\angle AOE = \\angle AOB + \\angle BAE = 90^\\circ + 43^\\circ = 133^\\circ$.\nSince $\\angle BOE = 90^\\circ$, we have $\\angle COE = 180^\\circ - \\angle BCO - \\angle BOE = 180^\\circ - (90^\\circ - \\angle BAE) - 90^\\circ = 90^\\circ - 43^\\circ = 47^\\circ$.\nThen, $\\angle CED = \\angle COE - \\angle EOD = 47^\\circ - 90^\\circ = \\boxed{47}$.\nThe answer is: 47",
